 align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186479848 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "462afb47-f28d-50fb-a384-b84e85e58f07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479848 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186495250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186495193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494314 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b9d3e9cf-c6b8-5144-84b6-fb2bd0e11696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494533 #edb/ref 1080 "3-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494533 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494533 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6963f53e-90b3-59a4-b3ac-6bc885da9965" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494537 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494537 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186494537 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6b596b99-7294-5ff0-b898-15ee8d9ff660" #edb/ref 17592186045417]